Rewritten 2026-07-06 as an unordered backlog; completed work and its
rationale live in the git history of this file, docs/design/, and NEWS.

Items are listed alphabetically by plan name; the order carries no
meaning. Every item has an implementation plan in docs/plans/<name>.md,
and the planning/implementation/review process (who plans, who
implements, who reviews, which gates run) is docs/plans/README.md.
"window: pre-release" marks items whose cheap form expires when 1.0-0
freezes the R and dbarts.h compatibility contracts: they need a
go/no-go decision before submission, not necessarily the work itself.

Standing fact (VD, 2026-07-06): single-chain n >= 1e5 workloads are
common. The large-n performance items are live, not consumer-gated.

items
  architecture-doc: contributor-facing docs/architecture.md distilling
    the current engine design (layers, dispatch tiers, concepts, data
    model, mutation surface) out of the design docs' landing-note
    history; seeds from readability-review's current-state section.
  blocked-jacobi-trees: exact parallel tree updates via noise-splitting
    augmentation (per-tree pseudo-responses y_k ~ N(g_k, sigma^2/b),
    sum-constrained): b trees update independently per barrier at the
    cost of b-fold precision on structure moves. Candidate mechanism
    for within-chain-threading; an ESS-per-second experiment decides.
  bridge-error-path-leaks: Rf_error longjmps past the destructors of
    stack-owned C++ vectors in the bridge parsers/setters; found by
    the sanitizers valgrind leg's first run (2026-07-07, 31 blocks
    definitely lost across the suite's error-path tests). Fix so the
    leg gates green; setState's accumulator is the house pattern.
  capi-callbacks: additive dbarts.h evolution - per-sweep conditioning
    callback and observer hook at the existing pollInterrupt dispatch
    point; tau/groupEffects fields on dbarts_results.
  convergence-diagnostics: multi-chain fits return raw arrays with no
    R-hat/ESS story; posterior-package-compatible draw accessors and a
    summary that says whether the chains agree.
  data-ownership: own predictor storage instead of borrowing REAL(x)
    (drops the PROT_* pinning and the const_cast write-through);
    changes the documented aliasing of per-observation updates.
    window: pre-release.
  empty-leaf-veto: the -1e7 empty-leaf branch veto is a ported classic
    hack, redundant with the categorical gauge invariant; either
    occupancy-aware ordinal proposals or a documented, principled veto.
    Caution: -inf is not a drop-in (vetoed-vs-vetoed comparisons rely
    on the finite value; the gp-leaves deadlock).
  forest-split-bcf: BCF - prognostic + treatment forests - on the
    landed Forest split (steps 3-5: response model, formats, exact
    gate); bartCause is the named consumer and VD maintains it. Open
    questions 3-4 in docs/design/bcf.md gate the BCF model choices.
  gp-followups: sampled lengthscales (theta prior, per-sample channels,
    real cost - not the mechanical follow-up the proposal suggested);
    low-rank kernels. decision/consumer-gated.
  group-by-exposure: public group.by beyond rbart_vi
    (grouped-random-effects.md; naming reserved). decision-gated.
  grouped-equivalence: equivalence scenario for grouped rbart_vi fits,
    only if a grouped refactor is planned.
  grow-from-root: XBART-style root-down tree sampling on the
    provisioned cut-scan kernel; the highest-ceiling large-n item and
    the realistic doorway to any GPU backend. memo + kernel prototype
    first.
  hot-layer-u8: FOLDED into data-ownership's owned container (VD
    2026-07-07, after phase-1 kernel measurements showed no standalone
    partition win); per-column widths land with the container and get
    re-measured end-to-end there.
  interaction-constraints: structured sparsity and interaction limits
    on the SplitSelector seam. consumer-gated.
  linear-leaf-reuse: score->draw crossproduct reuse (needs a per-node
    stats cache the design deliberately avoids) and within-sweep
    chol(V) reuse; measure before deciding.
  monotone-bart: shape-constrained fits via the tree-level leaf-draw
    hook the design provisioned.
  multi-forest-models: multinomial, heteroscedastic, hurdle - queued
    behind forest-split-bcf; one design note each when picked.
  mutation-journal: build-new-and-swap for setPredictor instead of
    copy-old-and-restore; cell-granular journal for the patch paths;
    document the cost contract per entry point.
  negative-binomial: count outcomes via the Polya-Gamma NB
    augmentation (the PG sampler already ships); the r update decides
    integer vs real shape - a caveat shared with weighted-binary.
  ordinal-outcomes: cumulative probit on the existing truncated-normal
    machinery plus a cutpoint block.
  pointwise-loglik: per-observation log-likelihood as a Results field
    (null-skip), unlocking loo/WAIC integration.
  prior-predictive: R-level verbs over the already-ported prior
    sampling entry points, for prior calibration workflows.
  python-bindings: post kernel-cleanups the engine is R-free below the
    bridge; a pybind11 facade wrapper becomes prototype-scale. horizon,
    likely out-of-repo. decision-gated.
  rbart-loop-profile: MEASURED 2026-07-07, verdict GO (overhead 15-76%
    across cells; table in the plan file). The fix rides
    capi-callbacks' conditioning hook; write that follow-up plan when
    capi-callbacks is picked. (The correctness bug this measurement
    surfaced was fixed as rbart-custom-prior-divergence, c7fa0e4.)
  readability-review: the bartcore branch was agent-written end to end;
    rubric-driven human-readability pass over its code, comments, and
    design docs (core-generalization.md's landing-note accretion
    especially). Also a standing review step in docs/plans/README.md.
  repo-modernization: standing hygiene bundle. Remaining: PR-gate the
    sanitizers workflow once the new gcc-asan/valgrind legs prove
    stable on pushes; optional codecov badge (VD's call); optional
    roxygen2 and NEWS.md migrations (do not start unasked).
  robust-errors: Student-t residuals as a scale-mixture on the
    workingWeights hook; composes with user weights.
  sparse-extensions: in-place mutation, sparse x.test, streaming range
    kernel, mutation on dense-backed mixed columns (sparse-columns.md
    landing notes). The u8 width entry moved to hot-layer-u8.
    consumer-gated.
  survival-models: AFT log-normal (censoring via truncated-normal
    latents; riAFTBART is the named consumer) and discrete-time hazard
    (person-period ingestion); the design note picks which lands first.
  test-suite-trim: the top four tinytest files carry half the suite's
    wall time (per-observation rollback trials, simd size grid,
    thread-pool setup); same contracts at ~20s. Added 2026-07-06 at
    VD's request.
  warm-starts: initialize a sampler's forest from a previous fit's
    saved trees; the flat replay and cut-mapping machinery exist, the
    verb does not.
  weighted-binary: integer-weight probit (exact via replicated latent
    draws, linear in total counts; threshold hybrid if that matters)
    and arbitrary real logistic weights (needs a real-shape PG sampler;
    IPW use is a pseudo-likelihood trap). decision-gated, post 1.0.
  within-chain-threading: previously assessed-and-deferred pending
    n >= 1e5 workloads, now confirmed common. Deterministic fixed-block
    reductions preserve thread-count invariance; the measurement
    interacts with hot-layer-u8 (same DRAM-bound regime) and competes
    with blocked-jacobi-trees as the mechanism.
  x86-simd: three linalg SSE2/AVX bodies are scalar with intrinsics
    commented out (predates the rewrite; the originals used
    non-temporal stores autovectorization cannot emit) - measure on
    x86, restore or delete; add misc_setIndexedVectorToConstant to the
    dispatch table; SSR SIMD leaf; Windows-arm64 NEON config.

release (deferred; the one ordered procedure, run when VD triggers it)
  note: the schedule/dispatch-only workflows (equivalence, rchk,
    revdep-smoke) cannot register or run until they exist on the
    default branch - GitHub binds schedules and dispatch to it. Their
    first live runs happen when bartcore merges to main; validate them
    then. (Push-triggered workflows shook out green 2026-07-07.)
  push dbarts 1.0-0 (branch bartcore) and stan4bart 0.0-13; submit both
    to CRAN together. bartCause is ready on branch dbarts-1.0 in
    ~/Repositories/bartCause (two commits, unpushed, checks Status OK):
    push and submit it after dbarts is accepted.
  before submission, resolve the window: pre-release decisions above
    (data-ownership, family-on-model, flat-format-v2 reporting,
    range-scaling, state-format-policy) - a documented "no" is a valid
    resolution.
  re-run the revdep sweep near submission (manual; the revdepcheck
    package is GitHub-only). 23 CRAN reverse dependencies; the
    2026-07-06 pass was clean or explained everywhere (stan4bart 0.0-13
    dev OK; bartMan/EBcoBART/funcml/glossa/nlfh/riAFTBART/voi OK with
    _R_CHECK_FORCE_SUGGESTS_=false; bartCause handled by its update;
    tidytreatment's WARNING is the documented ABI break, resolved by
    stan4bart 0.0-13; bartXViz not checkable locally - own gfortran
    runtime, R-level dbarts use only; the 12 Suggests-level packages
    not individually checked).
  write cran-comments.md at submission time. Content it needs: major
    release, engine rewritten, seeded results change; the C++ interface
    is removed and dbarts.h replaces it, so stan4bart 0.0-12 cannot
    build against 1.0-0 and 0.0-13 is submitted alongside (same
    maintainer); revdep summary as above; test environments; goal
    0 errors / 0 warnings / 0 notes.
  stan4bart follow-up: adopt categorical splits (it pins factors =
    "indicators"); lockstep with the dbarts release.
  optional courtesy: notify the tmle maintainers. Their default
    SuperLearner dbarts wrappers pass obsWeights unconditionally and
    pnorm() the latents; unit weights are handled dbarts-side now, but
    genuinely weighted binomial analyses lose the dbarts learners by
    design, and family routing on their side would need the matching
    inverse link.
